From: MediaTek vendor feed <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: fix VLAN deletion to override the FID

Port of MediaTek vendor patch 999-dsa-06 (mtk-openwrt-feeds,
25.12/files/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12), unmodified - applies
cleanly to this tree's drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c, no chip-version gate.

Fix mt7530_hw_vlan_del() to explicitly set FID(FID_BRIDGED) when
updating a VLAN entry that still has port members after deletion.
mt7530_hw_vlan_add() already sets FID(FID_BRIDGED) on the same VAWD1
register format (see the sibling call a few lines up in this file);
mt7530_hw_vlan_del() omitting it left a stale/undefined FID hardware
group behind a partial VLAN-member deletion on the exact MT7531 DSA
switch this board uses (4x LAN + 1x WAN).

See docs/README.md's patch map.

Signed-off-by: MediaTek vendor feed <noreply@example.invalid>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
@@ -1742,7 +1742,7 @@ mt7530_hw_vlan_del(struct mt7530_priv *
 
 	if (new_members) {
 		val = IVL_MAC | VTAG_EN | PORT_MEM(new_members) |
-		      VLAN_VALID;
+		      FID(FID_BRIDGED) | VLAN_VALID;
 		mt7530_write(priv, MT7530_VAWD1, val);
 	} else {
 		mt7530_write(priv, MT7530_VAWD1, 0);
